# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.79, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.78.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.79 is the FIRST cut since v1.0.77 with a changed payload, and both 
#   changes exist because the v1.0.78 cold walk could finally see them. CM051 
#   #1848 creates the qdrant collections where store readiness is PROVEN 
#   rather than on a one-shot 300s cap, and re-checks PER NAME because a 
#   cardinality test cannot see a missing member; it closes a RECURRENCE that 
#   install.sh:29350 already records from the v1.0.60 walk. CM051 #1850 
#   re-arms the store curl credential after the promote: the array was armed 
#   with -K into the /tmp staging tree, promote deleted that tree, and every 
#   later credentialed curl exited 26 against a store that answered 9971 
#   times with 200. CM051 #1849 is harness-only and makes the walk wait for 
#   each people store to STOP MOVING before the two reconcile probes run, 
#   gating on per-store stability rather than on the two stores agreeing, 
#   which would have been a fixture. DAEMON_COMMIT is unchanged at e3ddf5de 
#   (hub-v0.4.75, tarball b2e58127), so no daemon rebuild is involved and the 
#   Q1 grounded FAIL is expected to remain. This cut is NOT a CLEAN 
#   candidate: three FAIL rows are predicted in cut-manifests/v1.0.79.yaml 
#   before the tag.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.80, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.79.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.79 was walked twice and failed both times. This cut carries the two 
#   install.sh fixes those walks grounded, plus the daemon pin, and it is the 
#   first cut whose payload changes since v1.0.79. CM051 #1856: the workspace 
#   marker published a /tmp/ostler-prelaunch-<pid> path that the promote then 
#   deleted, the sixth instance of the staging-path class install.sh names at 
#   :353 and :13963. CM051 #1857: the flat 300s contact-merge budget killed 
#   its own converge at the cap on the v1.0.79 box (waited_s=300 
#   budget_s=300); it is now derived from the person count in the graph this 
#   install built, with K measured from that box's own catch-up log at 1822 
#   persons in 919s, and the reader runs the bundled venv interpreter because 
#   /usr/bin/python3 is a CLT stub that returns non-zero and aborted the 
#   install under errexit. Daemon 0.4.76 (ostler-assistant 42abcf8a): a reply 
#   that is, whole and trimmed, a tool call is dispatched instead of shipped 
#   to the customer as the answer. NOT expected clean: 
#   usage_journal_producers stays FAIL with three producers out of repo and a 
#   fourth unmeasurable by construction, and assistant_answers_grounded loses 
#   one of its three reasons rather than passing. The two rows in play are 
#   converge_kill_is_recorded and people_stores_reconcile.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.81, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.80.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.80 WAS TAGGED ONCE AT a467cc29 AND BUILT NOTHING. Preflight succeeded;
#   the cut job failed in eleven seconds at "Build, sign, notarise, staple".
#   v1.0.81 carries that payload UNCHANGED plus the one pin that stopped it.
#
#   TWO CAUSES, and the second is why the version was spent rather than delayed:
#   (1) the cut fetches TWO artefacts at the SAME tag string from DIFFERENT
#   repos -- the daemon from ostler-ai/ostler-releases (gui/Makefile:262
#   DAEMON_REPO) and Ostler.app from ostler-ai/ostler-assistant (:305
#   HUB_APP_REPO) -- and only the first had been published. (2) HUB_APP_SHA256
#   still named the 0.4.75 bundle, and download-hub-app verifies fail-closed,
#   so publishing the bundle only moved the failure from the fetch to the
#   checksum. Moving a pin is a CM051 commit and a tag cannot take one.
#
#   SO THE PAYLOAD IS: CM051 #1856 (the workspace marker names the promoted tree,
#   not the /tmp staging one the promote deletes), CM051 #1857 (the contact-merge
#   budget derived from the person count in the graph this install built, with the
#   reader on the bundled venv interpreter because /usr/bin/python3 is a CLT stub
#   that aborted the install under errexit), daemon 0.4.76 at ostler-assistant
#   42abcf8a (a reply that is, whole and trimmed, a tool call is dispatched rather
#   than shipped to the customer), and NEW for this cut CM051 #1863: HUB_APP_SHA256
#   1bad546c -> 2e2e5ea9, naming the Ostler.app bundle actually published for
#   0.4.76. Four BOM rows: the three carried forward unchanged, plus the pin.
#
#   NOT EXPECTED CLEAN, and Andy is not asked to walk on this forecast. Two rows
#   are in play: converge_kill_is_recorded and people_stores_reconcile.
#   usage_journal_producers is forecast FAIL and non-blocking -- its item 5
#   allowance is UNSPENT because v1.0.80 never cut. assistant_answers_grounded
#   loses one of its three reasons and does not pass.
#
#   ⚠️ THIS BLOCK WAS FIRST WRITTEN WITH v1.0.80's REASON, VERBATIM. The --reason
#   text was drafted into a scratchpad file for v1.0.80 and passed to new_cut.sh
#   again for v1.0.81 without being re-read, so cut.env claimed this was the first
#   payload change since v1.0.79 and never mentioned the hub app -- contradicting
#   the BOM, the manifest, the ledger row and the rollforward row, all of which
#   said it properly. Caught by TNM diffing this block against v1.0.80's. A
#   prepared artefact reused unread is the same defect as a register unread, which
#   is the one that cost v1.0.80.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
